<title>USA: Quick &amp; Reilly Group Inc Q4 net falls.</title>
<headline>Quick &amp; Reilly Group Inc Q4 net falls.</headline>
<dateline>PALM BEACH, Fla. 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fourth Quarter Ended</p>
<p>					     02/28/97     02/29/96</p>
<p> Gross Revenues		    $139,648,016 $129,673,919</p>
<p> Net Revenues			 103,561,875  101,606,142</p>
<p> Net Income Before Income Taxes  39,025,849   40,038,637</p>
<p> Net Income			    23,213,297   25,397,880</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share			  0.92	   1.01</p>
<p>Average Number of Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding			   25,179,69   25,082,030</p>
<p>						     Year Ended</p>
<p>						02/28/97     02/29/96</p>
<p> Gross Revenues		     $507,032,147 $443,865,021</p>
<p> Net Revenues			  379,412,379  324,600,196</p>
<p>Net Income Before Income Taxes  139,176,098  122,215,888</p>
<p> Net Income			     82,019,484   69,443,572</p>
<p> Earnings Per Share			   3.26	   2.78</p>
<p>Average Number of Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding			    25,176,79   24,985,177</p>
<p> Book Value Per Share			14.85	  12.00</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q4 earnings per share would have been $.86, rather than $1.01, if not for the realization of tax savings, and a freeing of reserves due to actuarial experience with the company's self-insurance programs.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
